  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of children with blue eyes and the number of children with brown eyes by rounding to the nearest $10$:\n\n- number of children with blue eyes: $22⟶20$\n\n- number of children with brown eyes: $35⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of children with blue eyes to the number of children with brown eyes is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{40}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{2}{4}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2÷2}{4÷2}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of children with blue eyes to the number of children with brown eyes is approximately $\\frac{1}{2}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
